From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsCommitDiag <kms-diag@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 11:30:00
Subject: [PATCH 0140] gpu31-kms: instrument the atomic commit/check path (int90)

KWin initialises (AMS, planes, GPU, GL, output) and then its first atomic
commit fails with EINVAL; the only visible line is the pre-swap state dump.
This patch is diagnostic only (no behaviour change) and closes every gap
between the ATOMIC ioctl and the first DECON register write:

- core `drm_atomic_plane_check()`: print the whole incoming plane state
  (plane id, crtc, fb, format, src 16.16, dst) and every rejection reason with
  values (both-set rule, possible_crtcs mask, format table, coordinate
  overflow, source outside fb).  These were DRM_DEBUG_KMS, invisible at the
  production log level.
- core `drm_atomic_crtc_check()`: print active/enable/mode_changed/
  active_changed and the active-without-enable rejection.
- `drm_atomic_check_only()`: print the driver's atomic_check rc together with
  allow_modeset, and the "requires full modeset but allow_modeset=0" rejection
  with the CRTC's changed bits (the ATOMIC flags KWin passed are the likely
  EINVAL source).
- `exynos7580_atomic_check()`: dump every plane/crtc state in the incoming
  changeset before and after `drm_atomic_helper_check()`.
- `exynos7580_atomic_commit()`: stage logs for enable_link, prepare_planes,
  swap_state and commit_tail, plus the full state dump on entry and on a
  prepare_planes failure.
- `exynos7580_plane_atomic_check()`: print the state, max_win, the
  state_to_win rc and decoded destination; every `exynos7580_check_rect()`
  rule now logs its failing values; the fractional 16.16 source rule logs the
  raw values.
- `exynos7580_fb_scanout()`: log fb/plane/format/pitch, bad fb/plane and the
  final rc/address.

Runtime: KWin's failing commit produces either a core rejection line (with the
exact rule and CRTC bits) or the driver stage/plane line, which identifies the
failing check and the values to relax.  All prints are one line per
commit/plane and removable in a single hunk group.

